// Exercise 5.1 - two bricks first, then a third.
//
// The quality lenses of the case study are argued in ../bricks/, one file each. None of
// them mentions the others. Your job is to gather them under a single claim without
// editing any of them.
//
// Two of the three are loaded below. The third is yours to load, in step 2.
//
// Check your work with:   jpipe diagnostic -i 01_assemble.jd

load "../bricks/fair.jd"
load "../bricks/performant.jd"

// TODO 1. write a justification named `deployable` that assembles the two bricks above.
//
//         justification <name> is assemble(<brick>, <brick>) {
//             conclusionLabel: "..."
//             strategyLabel:   "..."
//         }
//
//         Let the editor write most of it: type `is ` and press ⌃Space for the operator,
//         press it again inside the parentheses for the models in scope, and again inside
//         the braces for the keys assemble requires.
//
//         assemble does not invent the new claim for you. The conclusion is what these
//         lenses together let you say, and the strategy is why those are the right ones.

